 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Part four. Day nine. I had not spoken out loud since it used my sister's voice.",
   "pausa": 0.8,
   "vel": 0.88
  },
  {
   "texto": "This morning, the elevator lights came back on.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "Boots in the stairwell. Radios. Heavy tools.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A man shouted: rescue team. We are opening the door now.",
   "pausa": 0.9,
   "vel": 0.85
  },
  {
   "texto": "And that is when I finally understood why I was still alive.",
   "pausa": 0.8,
   "vel": 0.84
  },
  {
   "texto": "Real rescuers never ask you to open it. They open it themselves.",
   "pausa": 1.0,
   "vel": 0.82
  },
  {
   "texto": "The thing outside had asked me. Every single night.",
   "pausa": 1.0,
   "vel": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "Going down, we passed every other elevator. All of them open. All of them empty.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "If you are hearing this from inside one: do not answer. Wait to be opened.",
   "pausa": 0.5,
   "vel": 0.84
  }
 ],
